From c307a9d0add1e05ac2e53abd51db3afd9013b4e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:48:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp): set work offsets, setups, the machine and fixtures

The MCP server could set stock but not the rest of a setup. Nine new
tools, each one existing command run through the session History (so
undo/redo walk them) with every refusal returned as a tool error:

- add_setup / activate_setup (CreateSetup / ActivateSetup)
- set_wcs (SetWcsOrigin): an absolute origin, or a min/center/max point
  of the active setup's stock box plus an optional offset - "G54 off
  the stock corner" in one call; an omitted rotation keeps the current
- set_work_offset (SetSetupWorkOffset): the G54-G59 word a setup posts
- load_machine (LoadMachine, or SetSetupMachine for one setup): a
  built-in by name, a .mch file, or clear
- add_fixture / remove_fixture / move_fixture (TagFixture /
  UntagFixture / MoveFixture)
- get_fixture_findings: every setup's fixtures and machine table with
  their boxes, and each live toolpath collision as data (op, move,
  struck part, message, blocks_post)

posting::fixture_problems is split into fixture_findings (the hits as
data) and the gate's string form, so the tool and the post gate read
one walk; the gate's behaviour is unchanged. The new handlers live in
mcp/setup_tools.rs and mcp/fixture_tools.rs; tools.rs chains their
tables rather than growing its own. Pinned by the new mcp_setup suite.

Fixes #181

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
